steps:
["First, let's determine how many pieces Kalinda and her mom can place together per minute.", "Kalinda places 4 pieces per minute. Her mom places half as many pieces as Kalinda, so her mom places \(4 \div 2 = 2\) pieces per minute.", "Together, they place \(4 + 2 = 6\) pieces per minute.", "Next, we need to find out how many minutes it will take them to place all 360 pieces. We do this by dividing the total number of pieces by the number of pieces they can place together per minute:", "\[
\frac{360}{6} = 60 \text{ minutes}
\]", "Since there are 60 minutes in an hour, we convert the time from minutes to hours:", "\[
\frac{60}{60} = 1 \text{ hour}
\]"]
